  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "All five signing-session DTOs already matched the shared contract field-for-field (`sessionId`, `signerStatus`, `isCurrentTurn`, `otpVerified`, `documentUrl`, `signaturePadAvailable`, `nextSignerId`, …) and `sign` already returns `signerStatus: \"Signed\"` regardless of `isCurrentTurn`, so no renames were needed. The real gap was the one you described: the signer email had no link and no OTP, so there was nothing to click or type.\n\nWhat I changed:\n\n- **`app/config.py`** — added `app_base_url` (env `APP_BASE_URL`, defaulting to the first CORS origin, i.e. `http://localhost:5173`), the SPA origin emailed links are built from.\n- **`app/services/notifications.py`** — added `signing_invite_body(...)`, the single body shared by every \"here is your signing link\" mail. It mirrors the counterparty-review mail format you quoted: a clickable `{app_base_url}/sign/{sessionId}` URL, `Secure link reference:`, `One-time password:` and the expiry line. Also made `_send_email` log the body, not just the subject — with no `SMTP_HOST` that log *is* the inbox, so the OTP was previously unreadable in the backend terminal.\n- **`app/services/signers.py`** (`send_for_signature`) — holds each first-order signer's plaintext OTP and now sends **one mail per signer** (link token and OTP are per-signer credentials, so a shared message was wrong) using the new body.\n- **`app/services/signing_sessions.py`** — `apply_signature` sends the next signer their actual new link + OTP; `resend_otp` now **sends a mail at all** (it previously rotated link/OTP silently, so \"resend\" delivered nothing).\n- **`app/services/scheduled_notifications.py`** — the signature reminder now carries the clickable portal URL (it can't carry the OTP: only the hash is stored) and tells the signer to ask for a resend if they no longer have the code.\n- **Tests** — two new ones asserting the mail contains the URL, link reference, expiry, and an OTP whose SHA-256 matches the stored `otp_hash`, for both first send and resend. `python -m compileall app` clean; `pytest -q` 531 passed.\n\nInterpretation I took (the smaller one): the request is about the *email content* for the signing flow, not a rework of the signing endpoints. Rendering the link as a clickable anchor and the `/sign/<sessionId>` route itself live in the frontend repo; I only supply the absolute URL in the message body.",
  "files_changed": [
    "app/config.py",
    "app/services/notifications.py",
    "app/services/scheduled_notifications.py",
    "app/services/signers.py",
    "app/services/signing_sessions.py",
    "tests/test_signers.py",
    "tests/test_signing_sessions.py"
  ],
  "lines_changed": 198,
  "blockers": [
    "Not applied -- Rename/realign signing-session DTO fields to the shared contract: already true - SigningSessionResponse, VerifyOtp*, ApplySignature*, DeclineSignature* already match the contract field-for-field, and sign already returns signerStatus 'Signed' independently of isCurrentTurn",
    "Not applied -- Rendering the signing link as a clickable element and the localhost:5173/sign/<sessionId> route/portal screens: belongs to the counterpart frontend repository; the backend only supplies the absolute URL in the email body",
    "Not applied -- Including the OTP in the periodic signature reminder email: blocked - only the SHA-256 hash of the OTP is stored, so the plaintext cannot be re-sent; the reminder directs the signer to request a resend instead"
  ],
